      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The Seattle real estate market is a bit like a bustling market where the local goblins are the ones doing the actual trading, but they don't have the authority to sign the final contracts, so they need a neutral third party to hold the keys and the money until the deal is absolutely certain. That neutral third party is your escrow agent, and they are essentially the most boring, unexciting goblin in the entire world because they just sit there counting coins and watching paperwork while the other goblins (the buyers and sellers) do all the exciting stuff.\n\nSo, when you see \"escrow\" everywhere in your contract, it's just the goblins' way of saying, \"We are holding your money in a special vault until we are 100% sure the house is actually yours.\" They need to hold your money for a while because, in this goblin world, things can go wrong at any second. Maybe the seller's goblin decides to sell to a higher bidder, or maybe the seller's goblin decides to sell to a goblin from a different dimension who doesn't know the rules. If the seller's goblin tries to sneak away with the house before the buyer's goblin has paid,",
